  "verdict": "SMOKE-VALIDATED (machinery + wall-#1 handling) -- the pipeline runs end-to-end on a real SimulationBridge; the recurrent synapses MOVE under the committed BDSP rule (plastic mean|dw| 0.02682 > 0.0001); the DIRECTED apical credit is ISOLABLE in the soma_g sweep -- at g=0 (decoupled) B stays 0 and directed==lesion (the documented boundary), and turning on bdsp_apical_couples_soma raises measured bursts B monotonically with g and steers the weight move up to 6.7x the apical=0 lesion. LESION-BUG FIX (this build): the arm was named 'apical_lesion' but the teach checked mode=='lesion' -> the lesion ran the FULL directed apical (== plastic); corrected to a TRUE apical=0 lesion. With it, the CORRECTED apical_lesion arm (apical=0) shows the DIRECTED credit DOMINATES the undirected -Pbar*E drift (plastic directed |dw| 0.02306 = plastic 0.02682 - lesion 0.00376, ~6.1x the undirected drift), and the drift is METRIC-INERT (lesion CE 1.524 ~ fixed 1.523) -- so plastic is NOT swamped by drift; it moves the weights in the credited direction but that reservoir change yields only a MARGINAL read-out CE gain (plastic 1.520 vs fixed 1.523) at this scale. A clean within-horizon CE-win still needs the sparser bursting regime + lr/epoch tuning = the controller's sweep. NOT a faked positive. || MICROCIRCUIT (D1 clean-error variant): resid_frac 0.924 (1=no-cancel/0=full-cancel) -- the SST-like interneuron cancels only ~8% of the top-down, because the raw apical is ALREADY the FA error k*(Y@delta) and its target-innovation is NOT linearly predictable from the reservoir rate r_t. Mechanistically the microcircuit branch modifies ONLY the effective apical (raw - int_drive); it does NOT touch the -Pbar*E weight-update baseline, so it CANNOT reduce the undirected drift. Its lower total |dw| (0.02175 vs plastic 0.02682) = a WEAKER directed credit (micro directed |dw| 0.01799 = 0.78x plastic's 0.02306; fewer directed bursts), NOT drift cancellation. On CE: micro overall 1.511 vs fixed 1.523 vs plastic 1.520; within-horizon(d3-6) micro-minus-fixed -0.02695 vs plastic 0.0037. => HONEST READ: micro's overall+within-horizon CE edge over fixed is present but TINY and 1-seed (single-bucket-driven), and it comes at the cost of a weaker directed credit -- NOT a robust CE-win. The interneuron-as-literally-wired barely cancels (the apical is already the clean error), so it is ~plastic-with-a-slightly-weaker-credit. NOT a faked positive; see the finding for the diagnosis."
